1
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:07,880
O sunar za no to rai za auga.

2
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,150
Whoa.

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,800
Everything looks way brighter now.

4
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:16,060
So this is night vision magic.

5
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:19,317
I guess spriggans are good
for something after all.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,224
I don't know if that was
a compliment or a diss.

7
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:24,737
You're practicing the magic you can use.

8
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,877
That's the important thing.

9
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,717
And projecting illusions
is one of your specialties.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:29,630
Illusions?

11
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:30,968
Yeah, to trick people with.

12
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:34,177
It's cool, but it's not gonna
help anyone much in combat.

13
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:37,197
But you never know in a
life-or-death situation

14
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,456
your lame spriggan magic
might actually come in handy.

15
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,480
Now that was a diss.

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:12,780
Of Me Make a mistake Allow we run it

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,920
The darkness I find

18
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,500
Don't make me out where I am

19
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:27,380
I will Look the future

20
00:01:49,260 --> 00:01:53,940
If you're just a little bit,
you'll be able to do it.

21
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:59,940
If you're in the middle of the
sky, you'll be able to fly.

22
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:07,480
If you're in the middle of the
future, you'll be able to fly.

23
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,917
No, you're just memorizing the words.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,517
You have to learn what the
words of power mean first,

25
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,577
then match them with the
effects of the magic.

26
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,484
That's how you memorize spells.

27
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:34,477
I never thought I'd be in a game and have

28
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:37,148
to memorize words from
a different language.

29
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:42,520
Oh, and just so you know, the higher-ranked
spells have about 20 words. Holy crap.

30
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:44,817
I'll just stick to fighting then.

31
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,488
Would you quit complaining?

32
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:49,357
Oh, someone's messaging me.

33
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,760
Sorry, I have to get this. Sure.

34
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,880
It's Recon again.

35
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:56,927
It's probably nothing,
but I'll check anyway.

36
00:02:57,220 --> 00:03:00,900
It says, I was right, be careful, S.

37
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,080
That's it.

38
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,380
What's that mean? S?

39
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:07,340
Sa-shi-su-oh.

40
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:08,870
What's wrong?

41
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,080
Oh, nothing.

42
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:13,017
Daddy, I'm picking up movement behind us.

43
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:14,159
Are they monsters?

44
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:19,420
Uh-uh. They're players. A lot.
Twelve total. You're kidding.

45
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:23,300
I've got a bad feeling about this.

46
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,820
We better take cover.

47
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,500
Okay, but where?

48
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,280
Just leave everything to me.

49
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,780
Hey, easy.

50
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:38,500
Sheik, Shalu, Obis, Grone, Loputo.

51
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,238
We can talk, but we have to
be really quiet about it.

52
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,497
Anything louder than a whisper,
and it's going to break the spell.

53
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:49,410
Okay.

54
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:51,521
They'll be coming into view soon.

55
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,500
What is that? You see it? Huh?

56
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:59,300
No, I can't see anything.

57
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,317
I can tell it's not a player.

58
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,620
It's got red eyes.

59
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:04,098
Kind of like a bat.

60
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:16,149
Why'd you break our cover?

61
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:19,477
Because that thing out there is
a high-level tracing searcher.

62
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:20,854
We have to destroy it.

63
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,920
Eku, skicho, tutuge, tumala, Start.

64
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:31,040
Come on, we gotta go.

65
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,417
Can't we just hide behind
one of your spells again?

66
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,206
They already know we're here.

67
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,677
That tracer had us pegged.

68
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,797
Hiding's not going to do us any good.

69
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,760
Besides, that bat was a
fire element familiar.

70
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:45,637
That can only mean the ones
who are tracking us are...

71
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:46,860
The salamanders.

72
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:53,821
What's a party of salamanders
doing way down here?

73
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,511
Whoa, check out the lake.

74
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,777
Looks like we're going to get away.

75
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:06,389
Watch where you're
going or you'll fall in.

76
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,640
That won't work.

77
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,817
Why didn't you tell me that before?

78
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,724
Oh, right, like it's my
fault you're in a hurry.

79
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:26,547
It's an earth magic barrier.

80
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:29,137
You can bash on it all day
and it won't destroy it.

81
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:31,257
Can we jump in the lake
and swim around it?

82
00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:32,170
Nope.

83
00:05:32,253 --> 00:05:34,537
At least, not unless you want to be lunch.

84
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,977
The water is filled with
high-level monsters.

85
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:41,060
The Undines are the only ones who
can take those kinds of things on.

86
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:44,026
Then I guess the only
option left is to fight.

87
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,695
I'm not going to argue with
that, but it won't be easy.

88
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:51,637
If the Salamanders have high-level
earth magic, it can only mean one thing.

89
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:54,073
They have a powerful mage on their side.

90
00:05:56,660 --> 00:06:00,537
Leafa, I know you're good with the
sword, so don't take this the wrong way.

91
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:03,032
But could you back me up from here on in?

92
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:06,920
I need you to stay behind
and focus on healing me.

93
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:10,276
That way I can fight harder
and not worry about my HP.

94
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,760
They're targeting him
with everything they got!

95
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,900
Lisa Park!

96
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:43,040
Rando Doroto!

97
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:51,660
Lisa! Soap!

98
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:02,920
Su-fi-la-he-do-as-ta-lu-proto-supal-bani!

99
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,010
Uh-oh.

100
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,720
What do we do?

101
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,374
He's gonna run out of HP at some point.

102
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,240
That's enough, Kirito!

103
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:36,657
If we lose, it'll just mean a
couple extra hours of flying!

104
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:38,328
Let's give up while we can!

105
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,310
No way.

106
00:07:41,393 --> 00:07:45,066
As long as I'm alive, I'm not
gonna let anyone in my party die.

107
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,300
I won't let that happen again.

108
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,840
What the hell? What's he doing?

109
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,190
Hurry!

110
00:08:09,273 --> 00:08:10,437
This is your only chance!

111
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,517
What do you mean?

112
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:13,737
You have to use all the Main you have!

113
00:08:13,820 --> 00:08:17,317
Hurry and focus on shielding
him from the next magic attack!

114
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,230
Uh, okay.

115
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,480
But I don't think it's gonna help.

116
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:24,717
Deku, Baupa, Eugene,

117
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:28,460
Rando, Musti, Kara, Ressa!

118
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:36,900
Su, Shalu, Lindo, Ashnia, Batu, Emi, Ogu!

119
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:40,220
Mama, Sepa! Speldo!

120
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,680
Rando, Doroto!

121
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,980
Do it now, Daddy!

122
00:08:57,420 --> 00:08:59,140
He's using illusion magic.

123
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:03,664
But all that's going to do is make
him look like a giant monster.

124
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,620
Is that...Kirito?

125
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:39,490
Idiots!

126
00:09:39,573 --> 00:09:40,677
Don't break formation!

127
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,590
It's not real!

128
00:09:41,740 --> 00:09:42,637
Don't be afraid!

129
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:46,485
He can't hurt us if you stick to
the plan and stay in formation!

130
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,000
Hit him with an explosion spell!

131
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:04,040
Ayahu! Fala!

132
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,860
Fala! Hey Han!

133
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:22,990
Ah!

134
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,197
Retreat! Retreat!

135
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:32,500
RETREAT!

136
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:58,880
Stop it!

137
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:01,840
Wait, Kirito!

138
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,660
Hold on, don't kill him!

139
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:09,860
Isn't my daddy amazing?

140
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:11,800
Oh, my...

141
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:16,851
Okay, if you want to live, you better
tell me who sent you asshats after us.

142
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:18,050
Never.

143
00:11:18,133 --> 00:11:19,216
Kill me if you want.

144
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,320
You got it.

145
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:21,280
Oh, man.

146
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:22,900
Now that was cool.

147
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:29,260
That was an awesome fight. Huh?

148
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:31,517
Your plan wasn't shabby either.

149
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:34,857
If I was alone, I wouldn't have
lasted a minute against you dorks.

150
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:36,677
What are you telling him that for?

151
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:38,860
Let me handle this. Listen up.

152
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,217
I want to see if you
and me can make a deal.

153
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:42,130
Check it out.

154
00:11:42,213 --> 00:11:45,237
Those are all the items in Yul'd
I want after beating your asses.

155
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:48,657
All you have to do is answer my
questions and they could be yours.

156
00:11:48,740 --> 00:11:49,570
Sound good?

157
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,430
Seriously?

158
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:54,790
Totally.

159
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:00,470
Ugh, men.

160
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:02,675
It's like they forgot we're even here.

161
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:07,737
Earlier this evening, I got
an urgent text from Jitakasu.

162
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:11,017
He's the leader of the mage
squad, or, well, he used to be.

163
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:14,137
Anyway, I got this text telling
us all to meet him here.

164
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:18,457
And when I showed up, he said he needed
12 of us to go on a hunt for two players.

165
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,952
At first, I thought it was overkill, but,

166
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,700
well, he said you guys took
out Kagemune, so it made sense.

167
00:12:25,020 --> 00:12:26,497
Who's this Kagemune guy?

168
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:30,417
He's the leader of the Lancer Squad,
and he's known for hunting sylphs.

169
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:34,029
But yesterday, he got creamed
in a fight and had to retreat.

170
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,160
That was you guys, wasn't it?

171
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:41,457
Wait, why is Jitakasu so interested
in getting us out of the way?

172
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,357
Well, the order came from the top.

173
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:47,920
Something about you interfering
with the plan. Yeah? What plan?

174
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,780
Hey, hey, I'm just a grunt.

175
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,037
They don't tell me anything.

176
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:53,997
But I'm pretty sure something
really big's about to go down.

177
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,680
When I logged on today,

178
00:12:55,940 --> 00:13:00,980
I saw this big-ass swarm of salamander
troops heading up north. No way.

179
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:04,277
They're going to go try to clear
the world tree, aren't they?

180
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,220
I doubt that.

181
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:07,237
Someone figured that to take the tree,

182
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:09,677
the whole army would need
ancient weapon-class equipment,

183
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,584
and we can't afford that stuff.

184
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,598
That's everything I know, I promise.

185
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,577
You weren't lying about your
end of the deal, were you?

186
00:13:18,660 --> 00:13:19,490
No.

187
00:13:19,573 --> 00:13:21,440
I'm a man of my word, partner.

188
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:24,250
Hey,

189
00:13:24,333 --> 00:13:28,757
that big, ugly monster that was tearing
everything up, was that you or an illusion?

190
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,580
Yeah, I don't remember.

191
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,215
Wait, you don't know?

192
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,935
Not really, it just happens sometimes.

193
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,737
In the heat of battle, I'll snap
and can't remember a thing after.

194
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,980
Whoa, scary.

195
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:43,257
I think I remember most of what
happened this last time, though.

196
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:46,760
Like, I know I used that spell
Yui suggested. Do it now!

197
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:49,080
I also remember getting huge.

198
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,217
That was cool.

199
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:54,640
I remember losing my sword
and then grabbing people.

200
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:57,157
And you were chomping down
on them, remember that?

201
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:58,420
Oh, yeah.

202
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:03,080
I totally felt like a monster,
all eating people and everything.

203
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,940
So, uh, what did they taste like?

204
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:08,777
Kind of like grilled meat
just before it gets burnt.

205
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:09,857
All crispy and...

206
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:11,540
Okay, good. Sorry I asked.

207
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,110
Ow!

208
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:29,580
Wow, so this is LeGru.

209
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:32,120
Ow, that hurt.

210
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,097
Then you shouldn't be biting people.

211
00:14:34,180 --> 00:14:35,100
I'll say.

212
00:14:35,540 --> 00:14:37,457
Why is everyone ganging up on me?

213
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:40,237
I was trying to break the tension
with a stupid joke is all.

214
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:42,614
Bite me again and I'll cut you in half.

215
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,410
Yes, ma 'am.

216
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:47,800
Oh, look!

217
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,741
Hey, I just remembered something.

218
00:14:53,540 --> 00:14:57,657
Right before those salamanders attacked
us, you got a message from your friend.

219
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,460
Oh, I totally forgot.

220
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,038
Rekon's not online.

221
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,399
Maybe he's asleep.

222
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:07,337
Okay, well, why don't you
log out and give him a call?

223
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:09,417
Yeah, I think I better check in with him.

224
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:10,877
I'll only be gone a sec.

225
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,313
Wait for me here, okay?

226
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:16,260
Yui, would you please keep
an eye on my avatar? Me?

227
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:20,517
Yeah, I need to make sure your dad
doesn't mess around with it while I'm out.

228
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,659
Copy that, ma 'am.

229
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:23,215
You gotta be kidding.

230
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,060
Hey, Nagata.

231
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:53,557
What's with all the calls?

232
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:56,360
What do you want? You picked up! Finally!

233
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:58,113
Where were you, Suguha?

234
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:01,080
I was dealing with some in-game stuff.

235
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:02,640
We got trouble!

236
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:04,000
Like, big trouble!

237
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:06,777
Sigurd's coming after
us, and that's not all!

238
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:09,180
He betrayed Sakuya, the self commander!

239
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,380
Betrayed her? How?

240
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:15,057
Start from the beginning and
tell me everything that happened.

241
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,905
But we're running out of time!

242
00:16:17,740 --> 00:16:21,317
Okay, remember when the salamanders
ambushed us in the ancient forest?

243
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:23,277
Didn't that whole setup seem a little...

244
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:24,260
weird to you?

245
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,371
I don't know, not really.

246
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,117
Why do you think it was weird?

247
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:32,217
Remember how Sigurd said he'd be the decoy
and then he lured three of them away?

248
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:34,337
Yeah, now that you mention it...

249
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:36,017
Don't you think it was out of character?

250
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:39,159
I mean, usually he'd make
someone else do it, right?

251
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:40,780
Yeah, I guess.

252
00:16:41,940 --> 00:16:45,234
I mean, you're right, it's
weird, but what's your point?

253
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,780
Okay, here it is.

254
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:51,657
I found out he's been working
as a spy for the Salamanders,

255
